artifacts/WO-RUST-WAVE8-SETUP-01/review.events.jsonl:7:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat OWNER-DIRECTIVES.md && cat AGENTS.md && cat work/WO-RUST-WAVE8-SETUP-01.md && cat work/WO-RUST-SVG-ANIMATION-01.md && cat work/WO-RUST-NATIVE-BINDINGS-AUDIT-01.md'","aggregated_output":"# Owner directives (highest priority; supersede roadmap/CI/portability wording)\n\n1. **macOS only initially.** Apple Silicon, macOS 13+. No Linux or Windows code, CI jobs, runners, shims, packaging or portability work until the owner lifts this.\n2. Keep platform code isolated behind `platform/` interfaces (clean seams only; no stubs or ports for other OSes).\n3. CI/dev scripts target macOS only. Skip any roadmap item for Linux/Windows (M11, M12) and cross-platform CI matrices.\n\n4. **Full Rust port, owner direction2026-10-14.** Stop the former C implementation queue. Port all first-party application/platform/UI/parser/raster/document/animation/MCP code and in-repo development/test tooling to Rust, then complete the existing product finish line. This supersedes the C17 language/build lock and the former two-implementation-worker ceiling. Use as many useful disjoint Luna codex exec workers as available allowance/resources permit; preserve one writer per module and coordinator-only shared integration. Existing subscription allowance only, no extra credits/API billing. Preserve the current C code, unfinished candidates and evidence as migration references; no delete/reset or false completion claim. macOS13+ AppleSilicon, MPL2, custom UI, owned source-preserving SVG/XML parser/rasterizer, minimal reviewed/pinned dependencies, and no GPL editor source remain locked. Broad UI/E2E at the final stage; focused correctness checks continue.\n# Agent rules\n\nRead [OWNER-DIRECTIVES.md](OWNER-DIRECTIVES.md) first. It overrides conflicting\nroadmap and tooling text. Follow the active `work/WO-*.md`; inspect its allowed\nand protected paths before editing. Keep each work order buildable, tested,\nverified, and recorded in `STATE.md` and the ledgers.\n\n## Platform and product locks\n\n- Initial support is Apple Silicon macOS 13+. Do not add Linux/Windows code,\n  shims, CI jobs, runners, packaging, or portability work.\n- Keep platform implementations behind `platform/` interfaces; do not add\n  stubs for unsupported operating systems.\n- Rust for all first-party code is the active owner-approved migration target.\n  MPL-2.0, minimal pinned dependencies, custom-drawn UI, and an owned SVG\n  parser/rasterizer remain locked. Legacy C17 code is preserved as migration\n  reference; do not resume old C implementation orders. See ADR-0022.\n- Never read, fetch, or copy GPL SVG-editor source. Do not fetch external SVG\n  resources from the application. Record provenance for external algorithms.\n\n## Repository map\n\n- `app/`: executable composition.\n- `src/`: base, platform, XML/SVG, scene, raster, document, UI modules as added.\n- `docs/research-r4/`: authoritative operating model and roadmap.\n- `docs/research-r3/plan/`: architecture and coding guidance where r4 is silent.\n- `docs/adr/`: accepted decisions; `work/`: immutable ready work orders.\n- `tests/`: unit, property, fuzz, UI, and oracle tests as introduced.\n- `bench/`: corpus metadata, generators, runners, and results.\n- `artifacts/`: work-order evidence; `build/` and `.cache/` are generated.\n\n## Commands\n\nThe commands below are the preserved legacy C workflow. Rust workspace/build\ncommands become authoritative only through their implementation orders.\n\n- `./dev build`: configure and build Debug.\n- `./dev test-fast`: run local Python tests and validate the ledger.\n- `./dev verify`: run the Debug build and fast tests.\n- `cmake --preset mac-release && cmake --build --preset mac-release`: Release.\n- `python3 scripts/ledger.py validate ledger.jsonl`: validate work history.\n- `python3 -m unittest`: run Python harness tests when present.\n- `bench`, `fmt`, `lint`, `asan`, and `fuzz` become authoritative only when\n  their work orders implement them; do not claim missing commands run.\n\n## Engineering and safety\n\nUse the contracts in `docs/CODING_STANDARD.md`: explicit ownership, pointer+length\nslices, checked size arithmetic, bounded user input, no VLAs, and no unsafe\nstring functions. Preserve unknown SVG/XML source. Keep generated files in\nignored repo-local directories. Do not install system packages or touch sibling\ndirectories. Add dependencies only through an ADR and pinned provenance record.\n\nNever weaken frozen acceptance tests or oracles. Run commands named by the\nactive work order, then report exact evidence. Do not invent test or performance\nresults. Keep source files focused and under 800 lines; split cohesive modules\nbefore they grow further.\n\n## Rust migration execution\n\nFollow `docs/product/rust-port-goal-and-plan.md` and ready Rust work orders.\nMultiple Luna codex exec processes are authorized, with isolated current-source\nworktrees and disjoint modules; coordinator alone changes shared manifests,\nlocks, interfaces and ledgers. Use Low for inventory/docs, Medium for routine\nports, High for parser/renderer/concurrency/unsafe FFI. Escalate only on a named\nproblem; use the existing subscription allowance and no purchased credits.\nPreserve strict validation, original fixtures/assertions and byte-preserving\nround trips. Rust ownership replaces manual C ownership conventions; bounded\ninputs, checked arithmetic, safe cleanup and source limits still apply. Keep\nunsafe operations behind documented platform/FFI boundaries.\n---\nid: WO-RUST-WAVE8-SETUP-01\nrevision: 1\nstatus: READY\nmilestone: RUST-MIGRATION\nowner: project-owner\nexecutor: codex-coordinator\nbase_sha: 19234a036ed6a8d40c2ccdaec9b8186806d70eca\nspec_sha256: c323de1ad71fe8bda0a6d695b54efd0ef8546638bd4d4e0cffc695273b99ac2f\nparallel_safe: false\nnetwork: false\n---\n# Goal\nRegister one std-only SVG animation crate and freeze the full SMIL parse/eval\nscope plus native-binding audit. Accepted CSS is available; active source-editor\ncandidate remains isolated and is not consumed. Preserve the full product goal.\n\n# Files allowed to touch\n- `work/WO-RUST-WAVE8-SETUP-01.md`, `work/WO-RUST-SVG-ANIMATION-01.md`, `work/WO-RUST-NATIVE-BINDINGS-AUDIT-01.md`\n- `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`\n- `rust/crates/vexel-svg-animation/Cargo.toml`, `rust/crates/vexel-svg-animation/src/lib.rs`\n- `artifacts/WO-RUST-WAVE8-SETUP-01/**`\n- `artifacts/WO-RUST-WAVE7-SETUP-01/integrate_candidate.py` (exact accepted registration audit only)\n- `STATE.md`, `LEDGER.md`, `ledger.jsonl`, `docs/product/rust-port-goal-and-plan.md` (coordinator only)\n\n# Protected paths and contracts\nAll accepted Rust/source/assertions, original603legacy files, other manifests/\norders/evidence, active source-editor candidate and index/HEAD. New crate depends\nonly on accepted base/XML; no dependency on unfinished shape/editor/native\nports. One isolated LunaHigh animation writer; native binding audit is an\nindependent SolMedium documentation/evidence writer, no dependency adoption.\nNo system install, unsupportedOS, Cshim, stage/commit/reset/delete or broadUI/E2E.\nOlder editor integration accepts only exact accepted wave8 registration hashes.\nIndependent setup review required before implementation launch.\n\n# Verification\ncargo +stable generate-lockfile --offline\ncargo +stable check --workspace --locked --offline\npython3 scripts/wo_validate.py WO-RUST-WAVE8-SETUP-01 --ready\npython3 scripts/wo_validate.py WO-RUST-SVG-ANIMATION-01 --ready\npython3 scripts/wo_validate.py WO-RUST-NATIVE-BINDINGS-AUDIT-01 --ready\npython3 scripts/ledger.py validate ledger.jsonl\ngit diff --check\nExact Rust1.99/mac13/localcache; original603/index/acceptedRust preserved.\n\n# Output\nAccepted registrations/scopes only, fresh overlays and process registry; no\nmodule/app/performance or final acceptance claim.\n---\nid: WO-RUST-SVG-ANIMATION-01\nrevision: 1\nstatus: READY\nmilestone: RUST-MIGRATION\nowner: project-owner\nexecutor: codex-gpt-6-luna\nbase_sha: 19234a036ed6a8d40c2ccdaec9b8186806d70eca\nspec_sha256: be7604977c3a77e877eb7409159e277dc71617f172bb8301fbc6651abe58f16d\nparallel_safe: true\nnetwork: false\n---\n# Goal and full scope\nPort all of src/svg/animation/animation.h, animation_internal.h, smil.c,\nsmil_tracks.c, evaluate.c and motion_path.c into safe std-only Rust. Preserve\nall parse/evaluate/public helper semantics and original supported SMIL grammar,\nlimits (128 tracks, 256 values, 128 diagnostics, 3600 seconds, and every internal\nmotion/path/string bound), timing priority, diagnostic order/offsets, namespace\nand byte-span behavior, target/xlink resolution, syncbase graph/cycles,\nrepeat/duration/end/fill, set/animate/animateTransform/animateMotion,\nlinear/spline/discrete/paced modes, additive/accumulation flags, path structure\ncompatibility and numeric/color/transform/motion interpolation. No substitute\nsimplified timeline. Unsupported tracks are preserved/reported as the C scope\ndefines; raw source is never rewritten. Owned arrays plus a borrowed source or\nArc source owner with spans; no self-reference, unsafe, whole-source copies or\nquery-time parsing. Significant allocations fallible and capacity/resource\ncharges checked; document safe Rust adaptations explicitly without fake OOM.\nRejected parse/eval leaves no partial result. Define canonical new exported\nRust types so the renderer and authoring ports can consume this complete scope.\nPort all meaningful parse/eval assertions from tests/anim/test_animation.py and\nanimation_eval_cli.c, exact sample values/timing/attributes/active states; read\nall relevant project-authored fixtures, including both motion fixtures. Add\nexplicit bounds, unsupported/sync-cycle, source lifetime/spans and deterministic\nend/repeat/motion cases for public APIs. Render CLI assertions require the later\nfull renderer/CLI port and